Feature: Convert Spark SQL code to PySpark code
  As a data engineer
  I want to convert the provided Spark SQL code to PySpark code
  So that I can use it in a production environment

  Background:
    Given the Unity Catalog is "purgo_databricks"
    And the Unity Catalog Schema is "purgo_playground"
    And the target table path is retrieved using dbutils.widgets.get("target_table_path")
    And the partition key is retrieved using dbutils.widgets.get("partition")
    And the table format is retrieved using dbutils.widgets.get("table_format")
    And the compression is retrieved using dbutils.widgets.get("compression")
    And the table name is retrieved using dbutils.widgets.get("table_name")
    And the unity catalog is retrieved using dbutils.widgets.get("unity_catalog")
    And the environment is retrieved using dbutils.widgets.get("environment")
    And the project is retrieved using dbutils.widgets.get("project")
    And the load type is retrieved using dbutils.widgets.get("load_type")
    And the raw unity catalog is retrieved using dbutils.widgets.get("raw_unity_catalog")
    And the raw unity catalog hist is retrieved using dbutils.widgets.get("raw_unity_catalog_hist")
    And the config unity catalog is retrieved using dbutils.widgets.get("config_unity_catalog")
    And the edp lkp unity catalog is retrieved using dbutils.widgets.get("edp_lkp_unity_catalog")
    And the dims unity catalog is retrieved using dbutils.widgets.get("dims_unity_catalog")

  Scenario: Create DataFrames for each table
    Given the following tables:
      | table_name |
      | dw_ap_sla_aging_invoice_ca |
      | dw_party_d |
      | dw_supplier_site_d |
      | dw_internal_org_d_tl |
      | dw_ap_terms_d_tl |
      | dw_natural_account_d |
      | dw_gl_segment_d_tl |
      | dw_gl_code_combination_d |
      | edp_lkup |
      | fnd_flex_values |
      | fnd_flex_value_sets |
      | fnd_flex_values_tl |
    When I create a DataFrame for each table
    Then I should have a DataFrame for each table

  Scenario: Perform joins and transformations
    Given the DataFrames created in the previous scenario
    When I perform the joins and transformations defined in the Spark SQL code
    Then I should have a resulting DataFrame with the correct schema and data

  Scenario: Select final dataset
    Given the resulting DataFrame from the previous scenario
    When I select the final dataset
    Then I should have a final DataFrame with the correct schema and data

  Scenario Outline: Test different scenarios
    Given the following input data:
      | column1 | column2 |
      | value1  | value2  |
      | value3  | value4  |
    When I run the PySpark code with the input data
    Then I should get the expected output data:
      | column1 | column2 |
      | value5  | value6  |
      | value7  | value8  |

    Examples:
      | column1 | column2 | value1 | value2 | value3 | value4 | value5 | value6 | value7 | value8 |
      | foo     | bar     | 1      | 2      | 3      | 4      | 5      | 6      | 7      | 8      |
      | foo     | bar     | 9      | 10     | 11     | 12     | 13     | 14     | 15     | 16     |

  Scenario: Handle errors
    Given an error occurs during the execution of the PySpark code
    When I handle the error
    Then I should get an error message indicating the cause of the error

  Scenario: Optimize performance
    Given the PySpark code is optimized for performance
    When I run the optimized PySpark code
    Then I should get the expected output data in a shorter amount of time
